WEBVTT

1
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.720
You're my new partner.

2
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.080
That's right.

3
00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.200
Not the best way to meet with my head halfway down the toilet.

4
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.800
Doesn't exactly square with Teddy Daniels, the man,

5
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.160
the legend, I'll give you that.

6
00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.920
The legend?

7
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:20.920
What the hell you boys smoking

8
00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.480
over there in Portland anyway?

9
00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:23.960
Seattle.

10
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.620
I came from the office in Seattle.

11
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.860
How long you been with the marshals?

12
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.000
Four years.

13
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.600
So you know how small it is.

14
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.860
Sure.

15
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.740
How about you?

16
00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.620
You got a girl?

17
00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.620
May?

18
00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:56.020
I was.

19
00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.900
She died.

20
00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.380
Jesus.

21
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.980
There was a fire at the apartment building while I was at work.

22
00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.860
Four people died.

23
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.900
There was a smoke that got her, not the fire, so that's,

24
00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:11.700
that's important.

25
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.410
I'm sorry about some cigarettes.

26
00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.330
Oh, yeah.

27
00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.810
Have one of mine.

28
00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.130
Could've sworn they were in my jacket before I came home.

29
00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:27.360
Government employees are rocking blind.

30
00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.720
Thanks.

31
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.400
Give you a briefing about the institution before you left.

32
00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.030
All I know is it's a mental hospital.

33
00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.030
Probably the criminally insane.

34
00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.430
Well, if it's just folks running around,

35
00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.670
hearing voices, and chasing after butterflies,

36
00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.950
they wouldn't need us.

37
00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:56.290
Who are headed?

38
00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.290
Yep.

39
00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.450
The other side of the island is

40
00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.450
rock bluffs all the way down to the edge of the water.

41
00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.930
The dock, it's the only way on or off.

42
00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.970
We'll be casting off as soon as you two are ashore.

43
00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.610
I'd appreciate it if you'd hurry up about it.

44
00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:13.690
Why?

45
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:41.820
Storm's coming.

46
00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:46.100
Never seen a marshal's badge before.

47
00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.060
I'm Deputy Ward McPherson, gentlemen.

48
00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.340
Welcome to Shutter Island.

49
00:04:49.340 --> 00:05:04.700
I'll be the one taking you up to Ashcliffe.

50
00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.620
Boys seem a little on edge, Mr. McPherson.

51
00:05:07.620 --> 00:06:35.330
Right now, marshal, we all are.

52
00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.370
But during your stay, you will obey protocol.

53
00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.810
Is that understood?

54
00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.650
Absolutely.

55
00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:44.210
The red brick building on your right is Ward A, the male

56
00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.090
ward.

57
00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.530
Ward B, the female ward, is the one on your left.

58
00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:53.250
Ward C is that building on the bluffs, an old Civil War fort.

59
00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.730
The most dangerous patients are housed there.

60
00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.770
Admittance to Ward C is forbidden

61
00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.530
without the written consent and physical presence

62
00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:03.210
of both myself and Dr. Cawley.

63
00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.850
Is that understood?

64
00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:11.180
You could act like insanity is catching.

65
00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.980
You are hereby required to surrender your firearms.

66
00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:19.380
Mr. McPherson, we are duly appointed federal marshals.

67
00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.980
We are required to carry our firearms with us at all times.

68
00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:25.020
Executive Order 319 of the Federal Code of Penitentiary

69
00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.180
states that when inside a penitentiary,

70
00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.820
the offices of that institution

71
00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:33.460
have final authority.

72
00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.020
Gentlemen, you will not get through this gate

73
00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:57.020
with your firearms.

74
00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:57.860
OK.

75
00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.340
Now that the official stuff's done, come on, boys.

76
00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:14.380
What do you say we go find Dr. Cawley?

77
00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:15.940
When did she escape?

78
00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.060
This prisoner.

79
00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.300
I'm afraid Dr. Cawley will have

80
00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.340
to fill you in on the situation.

81
00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.300
Protocol.

82
00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.620
Correctional offices at a mental institution.

83
00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.820
That's a weird sight, if you don't mind me saying.

84
00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.260
It's the only facility of its kind

85
00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.300
in the US, even the world.

86
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.660
We take only the most dangerous

87
00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.940
damaged patients, ones no other hospital can manage.

88
00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.940
And it's all due to Dr. Cawley.

89
00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.820
He's created something really unique here.

90
00:08:37.820 --> 00:09:06.130
It's a hospital for people our society not only can fit.

91
00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:09.570
Top of his class at Johns Hopkins and have it.

92
00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:14.800
IDs, gentlemen.

93
00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.000
Show your badges, gentlemen.

94
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.040
Dr. Cawley's been consulted numerous times by Scotland

95
00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.880
Yard, MI5, the OSS.

96
00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.640
Why?

97
00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:27.540
What do you mean?

98
00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.700
What do intelligence agencies want to consult

99
00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:30.980
a psychiatrist about?

100
00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:43.060
I guess you'll have to ask him.

101
00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:43.980
Marshal Daniels?

102
00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.580
Doctor.

103
00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.580
Marshal Hall.

104
00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:48.580
Thank you, Deputy Walden.

105
00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.380
That'll be all.

106
00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.020
Yes, sir.

107
00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.740
Pleasure, gentlemen.

108
00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.460
He had a lot to say about you.

109
00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:57.620
MacPherson's a good man.

110
00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.700
He believes in the work we do here.

111
00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.180
And what would that be exactly?

112
00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:05.820
A moral fusion between law and order and clinical care.

113
00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:06.740
Pardon me, Doc.

114
00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:15.890
A what between what and what?

115
00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:18.970
Those paintings are quite accurate.

116
00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.010
Used to be the kind of patients we deal with here

117
00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:24.290
were shackled and left in their own filth.

118
00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.570
They were beaten as if whipping them bloody

119
00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:27.890
would drive the psychosis out.

120
00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.090
We drove screws into their brains.

121
00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.610
We submerged them in icy water

122
00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:36.570
until they lost consciousness or even drowned.

123
00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.570
And now?

124
00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.570
We treat them.

125
00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.890
Try to heal, try to cure.

126
00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.730
And if that fails, at least we provide them

127
00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:45.970
with a measure of comfort in their lives, calm.

128
00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:49.290
These are all violent defenders, right?

129
00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.730
I mean, they've hurt people, murdered them in some cases.

130
00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.170
In almost all cases, yes.

131
00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.770
And personally, Doctor, I'd have to say

132
00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:01.990
screw their sense of calm.

133
00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:04.350
It's my job to treat my patients, not their victims.

134
00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.750
I'm not here to judge.

135
00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.830
So this female prisoner?

136
00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.230
Patient.

137
00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.390
Excuse me, patient.

138
00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:16.510
One, Rachel Solando, escaped sometime in the last 24 hours.

139
00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.910
Last night, between 10 and midnight.

140
00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.550
Is she considered dangerous?

141
00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.270
You could say that.

142
00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:25.070
She killed all three of her children.

143
00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:27.990
She drowned them in the lake behind her house.

144
00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.710
She took them out one by one, held their heads

145
00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.390
under until they died.

146
00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.630
Then she brought them back inside

147
00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:34.390
and arranged them around the kitchen table.

148
00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:39.650
She ate a meal there before a neighbor dropped by.

149
00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:40.850
And what about the husband?

150
00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:41.810
He died.

151
00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.570
On the beaches at Normandy.

152
00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.330
She's a war widow.

153
00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.650
She starved herself when she first came here.

154
00:11:47.650 --> 00:12:00.420
She insisted the children weren't dead.

155
00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:01.580
Sorry, Doctor.

156
00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.220
You don't happen to have an aspirin, do you?

157
00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.900
Prime's the headaches, Marshal.

158
00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:07.220
Sometimes, but today I'm a little more

159
00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.340
prone to seasickness.

160
00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.220
Ah, dehydration.

161
00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.140
You all right, boss?

162
00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:11.940
Yeah.

163
00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.260
In that case, you're quite right.

164
00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:14.140
The simpler, the better.

165
00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.180
Well, thanks so much.

166
00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:20.780
Rachel still believes the children are alive.

167
00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:25.870
She also believes this place is her home in the Berkshires.

168
00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:26.670
You're kidding me.

169
00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:28.070
She's never once in two years

170
00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:29.950
acknowledged that she's in an institution

171
00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.070
she believes were all deliverymen,

172
00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:33.870
milkmen, postal workers.

173
00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.150
To sustain the delusion that her children never died,

174
00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.350
she's created an elaborate fictional structure

175
00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:42.630
and she gives us all parts to play in that fiction.

176
00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.750
So have you searched the grounds yet?

177
00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.430
The warden and his men scarred the island.

178
00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.510
Not a trace.

179
00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.110
What's more disturbing is we don't know

180
00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:54.070
how she got out of her room.

181
00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:57.950
It was locked from the outside and the only windows barred.

182
00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:10.140
It's as if she evaporated straight through the walls.

183
00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.580
Brought her right back here after group therapy,

184
00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:15.460
locked her in, came back for a midnight round,

185
00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:23.770
she was gone.

186
00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.450
Seriously, doctor, how is it possible that the truth

187
00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.090
never gets through to her?

188
00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:31.090
I mean, she's in a mental institution, right?

189
00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:33.330
Seems like something you've noticed from time to time.

190
00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.410
How many pairs of shoes are the patients given?

191
00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.890
Two pairs.

192
00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:38.610
Sanity's not a choice.

193
00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:41.810
Marshall, you can't just choose to get over it.

194
00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.530
What's up?

195
00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:44.810
She left here barefoot?

196
00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.610
Come on, doc, she couldn't get 10 yards in that terrain.

197
00:13:50.050 --> 00:14:10.390
Marshall?

198
00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.310
This is definitely Rachel's handwriting.

199
00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.270
I have no idea what the law for is, though.

200
00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:16.830
It's not a psychiatric term.

201
00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.190
I'm afraid not.

202
00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.590
Who is 67?

203
00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.190
Fuck if I know.

204
00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.350
I have to say, that's quite close

205
00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.710
to my clinical conclusion.

206
00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:28.030
Think it's just random scribblings?

207
00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:30.390
Oh, no, not at all, Rachel's smart.

208
00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.870
Brilliant, in fact.

209
00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.390
This paper could be important.

210
00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.390
Excuse me, doctor, but we're gonna have

211
00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.660
to hold onto this, of course.

212
00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.580
And you say she had to come through here?

213
00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:45.940
After lights out, the ordered is, play cards in here.

214
00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.460
Last night, there were seven men sitting at the base

215
00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.900
of those stairs playing stud poker,

216
00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.760
yet somehow Rachel managed to slip past them.

217
00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:57.720
How?

218
00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.000
She turns invisible?

219
00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.520
Doctor, we're gonna need access to the personnel files

220
00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.480
of all the medical staff, the nurses, the guards,

221
00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.440
the orderlies, anyone who was working there.

222
00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:09.280
We'll take your request under consideration.

223
00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:12.000
This is not a request, doctor.

224
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.560
This is a federal facility in a dangerous prison.

225
00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.800
Patient.

226
00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:18.200
Patient has escaped now.

227
00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:19.240
You will comply.

228
00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.680
All I can say is I'll see what I can do.

229
00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:24.560
Doctor, we're gonna need to speak with the staff.

230
00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:25.640
Do you understand?

231
00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:29.080
I'll assemble them in the common room after dinner.

232
00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.360
If you have any further questions,

233
00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:47.060
feel free to join the deputy warden in the search.

234
00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.700
It's 11 miles to the nearest land

235
00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.500
and the water's freezing.

236
00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:53.620
The current was strong last night, tide pushing in,

237
00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.340
sheet of ground had been crushed on the rocks

238
00:15:55.340 --> 00:16:01.510
and a body would have washed back up on shore.

239
00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:02.790
What about those caves down there?

240
00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.710
Have you checked them?

241
00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.150
No way she could get there.

242
00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.590
The base of those cliffs are covered

243
00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.590
in the poison ivy, live oak, sumac,

244
00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:14.990
and a thousand plants with thorns as big as my dick.

245
00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:23.520
You said yourself, Marshall, she's got no shoes.

246
00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:31.560
All right, let's check the other side.

247
00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:33.200
What's that tower?

248
00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.400
It's an old lighthouse.

249
00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:39.830
The guards already searched inside it.

250
00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:40.670
What's in there?

251
00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:42.110
More patients?

252
00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:43.630
Sewage treatment facility.

253
00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.710
It's getting dark soon.

254
00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.750
I'm calling this off for the night.

255
00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:54.310
Let's go, boys!

256
00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:56.190
You were on watch on the landing, huh?

257
00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:57.710
Yeah, couldn't nobody get in

258
00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:01.470
or out of their room on that corridor without me seeing.

259
00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:03.350
Okay, Rachel Solando,

260
00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:14.360
who else does she have to pass to get down here?

261
00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.200
Glenn Meade.

262
00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:18.280
Sir, I didn't see nothing.

263
00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.480
And you were at your post all night?

264
00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:24.760
Yeah, but I didn't see a thing.

265
00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:37.860
Glenn, Glenn, tell me the truth.

266
00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.660
I maybe went to the bathroom.

267
00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.500
What?

268
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.420
You breached protocol, Christ.

269
00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.900
I wasn't gone more than a minute.

270
00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.380
All right, let's back up here.

271
00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:48.900
Let's all just back up.

272
00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.340
Miss Solando was putting her room for lights out.

273
00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.700
Does anyone here know what she did before that?

274
00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:56.740
Anyone?

