00:35:36.380 --> 00:35:38.580
Axing him isn't the least understandable thing

553
00:35:38.580 --> 00:35:41.460
you could do.

554
00:35:41.460 --> 00:35:42.980
Maybe you shouldn't get out.

555
00:35:44.700 --> 00:35:46.100
What would I do if I did?

556
00:35:47.300 --> 00:35:49.140
I don't know the world anymore.

557
00:35:50.020 --> 00:35:51.860
They say there are bombs that can reduce

558
00:35:51.860 --> 00:35:53.940
whole cities to ash.

559
00:35:53.940 --> 00:35:55.420
And what do you call them?

560
00:35:55.420 --> 00:35:56.820
Televisions.

561
00:35:56.820 --> 00:35:59.340
Voices and faces coming from a box.

562
00:36:00.180 --> 00:36:02.100
I hear enough voices already.

563
00:36:03.420 --> 00:36:05.220
What can you tell us about Rachel?

564
00:36:08.590 --> 00:36:09.430
Not much.

565
00:36:09.430 --> 00:36:11.750
She keeps to herself.

566
00:36:11.750 --> 00:36:15.230
She believed her kids were alive.

567
00:36:16.030 --> 00:36:18.430
She thought she was still living in the Berkshires

568
00:36:18.430 --> 00:36:20.510
and we were all her neighbors.

569
00:36:20.510 --> 00:36:23.710
The milkmen, postmen.

570
00:36:23.710 --> 00:36:24.550
Delivery men.

571
00:36:26.110 --> 00:36:27.910
And Dr. Sheehan was there that night?

572
00:36:28.830 --> 00:36:29.670
Yes.

573
00:36:30.910 --> 00:36:35.190
He talked about anger.

574
00:36:35.190 --> 00:36:36.190
Tell me about him.

575
00:36:37.550 --> 00:36:40.820
What's he like?

576
00:36:40.820 --> 00:36:45.760
He's okay, nice.

577
00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:50.120
Not hard on the eyes, as my mother would say.

578
00:36:53.020 --> 00:36:54.740
Did he ever make a pass at you?

579
00:36:55.700 --> 00:36:56.540
No.

580
00:36:57.380 --> 00:37:04.040
No, Dr. Sheehan's a good doctor, you would know.

581
00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:06.400
Could I have a glass of water, please?

582
00:37:06.400 --> 00:37:22.630
No problem.

583
00:37:22.630 --> 00:37:28.950
Thank you, Marshall.

584
00:37:28.950 --> 00:37:31.910
I just have one more question for you, Mrs. Kearns.

585
00:37:31.910 --> 00:37:41.860
Did you ever meet a patient named Andrew Latus?

586
00:37:41.860 --> 00:37:51.820
No, never heard of her.

587
00:37:51.820 --> 00:37:53.620
She was coached.

588
00:37:53.620 --> 00:37:56.300
She was practically the same words as Cawley and the nurse

589
00:37:56.300 --> 00:37:58.140
like she'd been told exactly what to say.

590
00:37:58.140 --> 00:38:04.370
Who's Andrew Latus?

591
00:38:04.370 --> 00:38:06.770
Asked every one of those patients back there about him.

592
00:38:06.810 --> 00:38:12.590
Who is he?

593
00:38:12.590 --> 00:38:13.550
What the hell, boss?

594
00:38:13.550 --> 00:38:16.110
I'm your partner, for Christ's sake.

595
00:38:16.110 --> 00:38:17.190
We just met, Chuck.

596
00:38:18.510 --> 00:38:20.110
You've been on the beat for a long time.

597
00:38:20.110 --> 00:38:21.990
You got a duty, you got a career.

598
00:38:21.990 --> 00:38:26.460
What I'm doing, it's not exactly by the book.

599
00:38:27.940 --> 00:38:30.740
I don't give a damn about by the book, boss.

600
00:38:30.740 --> 00:38:37.940
I just wanna know what the hell's going on.

601
00:38:37.940 --> 00:38:39.820
When this case came over the wires,

602
00:38:41.500 --> 00:38:44.860
I requested it specifically, you understand?

603
00:38:44.860 --> 00:38:48.330
Why?

604
00:38:48.330 --> 00:38:52.130
Andrew Latus was a maintenance man

605
00:38:52.130 --> 00:38:59.540
in the apartment building where my wife and I lived, okay?

606
00:38:59.540 --> 00:39:04.260
He was also a firebug.

607
00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:09.680
Andrew Latus lit the match

608
00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:20.770
that caused the fire that killed my wife.

609
00:39:20.770 --> 00:39:24.890
Let him out!

610
00:39:24.890 --> 00:39:26.850
What happened to Latus?

611
00:39:26.850 --> 00:39:28.250
He got away with it.

612
00:39:28.250 --> 00:39:30.810
Latus got away with it and then he disappeared.

613
00:39:30.810 --> 00:39:32.690
About a year ago, I opened up the paper

614
00:39:32.690 --> 00:39:35.770
and there he is, ugly looking son of a bitch.

615
00:39:35.770 --> 00:39:38.490
Huge scar from his right temple down to his left lip,

616
00:39:38.490 --> 00:39:42.090
eyes different colors, not the type of face you'd forget.

617
00:39:42.090 --> 00:39:45.130
He burned down a schoolhouse, killed two people,

618
00:39:45.130 --> 00:39:47.050
said voices told him to do it.

619
00:39:47.050 --> 00:39:49.850
First he went to prison, then he got transferred here.

620
00:39:49.850 --> 00:39:50.850
Then what?

621
00:39:50.850 --> 00:39:52.130
Then nothing.

622
00:39:52.130 --> 00:39:55.930
He vanished like he never existed, no record whatsoever.

623
00:39:55.930 --> 00:39:58.730
Pretty sure he's not in Ward B, that leaves Ward C.

624
00:39:58.730 --> 00:39:59.770
I could be dead.

625
00:39:59.770 --> 00:40:02.490
So could Rachel Solando, for that matter.

626
00:40:02.490 --> 00:40:04.650
Lot of places to hide a body here.

627
00:40:05.850 --> 00:40:08.330
Only one place no one would really notice.

628
00:40:20.520 --> 00:40:24.400
That patient, Bridget Kern, when she sent me for water,

629
00:40:24.400 --> 00:40:27.440
she said something to you back there, didn't she?

630
00:40:27.440 --> 00:40:30.490
No.

631
00:40:30.490 --> 00:40:35.670
Come on, boss.

632
00:40:35.670 --> 00:40:54.140
She wrote it.

633
00:40:54.140 --> 00:40:55.540
We gotta get indoors!

634
00:40:55.540 --> 00:40:57.860
He's turning into fucking characters out here!

635
00:40:57.860 --> 00:40:58.700
Pull her!

636
00:40:58.700 --> 00:41:42.660
No, let's go!

637
00:41:42.660 --> 00:41:52.620
You okay, boss?

638
00:41:52.620 --> 00:42:00.030
So if Latus is here, what are you gonna do about it?

639
00:42:00.030 --> 00:42:09.900
I'm not here to kill Latus.

640
00:42:09.980 --> 00:42:23.520
If it wasn't my wife, I'd kill him twice.

641
00:42:23.520 --> 00:42:26.440
When we got through the gates at dark, Al,

642
00:42:26.440 --> 00:42:36.770
the SS guard surrendered.

643
00:42:36.770 --> 00:42:39.890
The commandant tried to kill himself before we got there,

644
00:42:39.890 --> 00:42:48.010
but he botched it, now to die.

645
00:42:48.010 --> 00:42:57.300
When we went outside, I saw all the bodies on the ground.

646
00:43:01.740 --> 00:43:39.500
Many to count, the guard surrendered.

647
00:43:39.500 --> 00:44:26.910
We took their guns, we lined them up.

648
00:44:26.910 --> 00:44:36.430
The warfare was dead.

649
00:44:36.430 --> 00:44:41.100
I've had enough of killing.

650
00:44:41.100 --> 00:44:44.170
That's not why I'm here.

651
00:44:44.210 --> 00:44:48.410
So what is this all about?

652
00:44:48.410 --> 00:44:51.570
After Latus vanished,

653
00:44:51.570 --> 00:44:54.210
I started doing some checking on Ashcliffe.

654
00:44:55.690 --> 00:44:57.370
A lot of people know about this place,

655
00:44:57.370 --> 00:44:59.130
but no one wants to talk, you know?

656
00:44:59.130 --> 00:45:04.780
It's like they're scared of something.

657
00:45:04.780 --> 00:45:07.300
You know, this place is funded by a special grant

658
00:45:08.740 --> 00:45:11.780
from the House Un-American Activities Committee.

659
00:45:11.780 --> 00:45:12.620
UAC?

660
00:45:12.620 --> 00:45:14.940
And how exactly are we fighting the commies

661
00:45:14.940 --> 00:45:16.700
from an island in Boston Harbor?

662
00:45:17.620 --> 00:45:20.060
By conducting experiments on the mind.

663
00:45:21.620 --> 00:45:23.220
At least that's my guess.

664
00:45:23.220 --> 00:45:25.060
And you think that's going on here?

665
00:45:25.060 --> 00:45:27.620
Like I said, no one would talk, right?

666
00:45:27.620 --> 00:45:30.380
Until I found somebody who used to be a patient here.

667
00:45:30.380 --> 00:45:32.500
Guy's name is George Noyce.

668
00:45:32.500 --> 00:45:34.820
Nice college kid, socialist.

669
00:45:34.820 --> 00:45:36.940
He gets offered some money to do a psych study.

670
00:45:36.940 --> 00:45:38.460
Guess what they were testing?

671
00:45:38.460 --> 00:45:39.540
Whose case?

672
00:45:39.540 --> 00:45:42.020
So he starts seeing dragons everywhere.

673
00:45:42.020 --> 00:45:43.980
He almost beats his professor to death.

674
00:45:44.300 --> 00:45:46.420
Ends up here in Ashcliffe.

675
00:45:46.420 --> 00:45:48.100
Ward C.

676
00:45:48.100 --> 00:45:50.620
They release him after one year, right?

677
00:45:50.620 --> 00:45:51.580
What does he do?

678
00:45:51.580 --> 00:45:54.780
Two weeks on the mainland, he walks into a bar,

679
00:45:54.780 --> 00:45:57.300
stabs three men to death.

680
00:45:57.300 --> 00:46:00.020
His lawyer pleads insanity, but Noyce,

681
00:46:00.020 --> 00:46:01.380
he stands up in the courtroom

682
00:46:01.380 --> 00:46:04.180
and he begs the judge for the electric chair

683
00:46:04.180 --> 00:46:06.180
anywhere but a mental hospital.

684
00:46:07.140 --> 00:46:09.380
Judge gives him life and dead in prison.

685
00:46:10.860 --> 00:46:11.980
And you found him?

686
00:46:11.980 --> 00:46:13.780
Yeah, I found him.

687
00:46:14.620 --> 00:46:18.090
Well, he's a mess.

688
00:46:18.090 --> 00:46:21.960
Pretty clear from what he tells me.

689
00:46:21.960 --> 00:46:24.040
What do you want people here?

690
00:46:24.040 --> 00:46:26.980
I don't know, boss.

691
00:46:26.980 --> 00:46:28.620
How do you believe a crazy guy?

692
00:46:28.620 --> 00:46:30.340
That's the beauty of it, isn't it?

693
00:46:30.340 --> 00:46:32.180
Crazy people, they're the perfect subjects.

694
00:46:32.180 --> 00:46:34.340
They talk, nobody listens.

695
00:46:35.220 --> 00:46:36.380
I stood at Dachau.

696
00:46:37.540 --> 00:46:41.860
We saw what human beings are capable of.

697
00:46:41.860 --> 00:46:44.580
For Christ's sakes, we fought a goddamn war to stop them

698
00:46:44.580 --> 00:46:48.380
and now I find out it may be happening here on our soil?

699
00:46:48.380 --> 00:46:50.620
No.

700
00:46:50.660 --> 00:46:52.620
So what are you really here to do, Ted?

701
00:46:53.980 --> 00:46:55.260
I'm gonna get the proof,

702
00:46:56.460 --> 00:46:57.900
I'm gonna go back

703
00:46:57.900 --> 00:46:59.980
and I'm gonna blow the lid off this place.

704
00:47:00.900 --> 00:47:01.740
That's it.

705
00:47:02.940 --> 00:47:03.900
Wait a minute.

706
00:47:05.060 --> 00:47:07.860
You started asking around about Ashcliffe,

707
00:47:07.860 --> 00:47:09.420
waiting for a chance to get out here

708
00:47:09.420 --> 00:47:13.230
and then suddenly they need a US Marshal?

709
00:47:13.230 --> 00:47:14.990
I got lucky, there was a patient escape.

710
00:47:14.990 --> 00:47:16.190
It was the perfect excuse.

711
00:47:16.190 --> 00:47:19.070
No, no, no, boss, luck doesn't work that way.

712
00:47:19.070 --> 00:47:20.870
The world doesn't work that way.

713
00:47:20.870 --> 00:47:24.230
They got an electrified fence around a septic facility.

714
00:47:24.230 --> 00:47:27.510
Ward C is inside a Civil War fort.

715
00:47:27.510 --> 00:47:30.070
A chief of staff that ties to the OSS.

716
00:47:30.070 --> 00:47:31.270
Funding from UAC.

717
00:47:31.270 --> 00:47:32.950
I mean, Jesus Christ.

718
00:47:32.950 --> 00:47:35.910
Everything about this place stinks of government ops.

719
00:47:35.910 --> 00:47:37.430
What if they wanted you here?

720
00:47:37.430 --> 00:47:38.270
Bullshit.

721
00:47:38.270 --> 00:47:39.270
You were asking questions.

722
00:47:39.270 --> 00:47:40.390
Bullshit. Bullshit.

723
00:47:40.390 --> 00:47:41.830
We came here for Rachel Salanda.

724
00:47:41.830 --> 00:47:44.870
Where was one shred of evidence she even existed?

725
00:47:44.870 --> 00:47:45.990
There's no way they could have known

726
00:47:45.990 --> 00:47:47.150
I'd be assigned to this case.

727
00:47:47.150 --> 00:47:47.990
There's no way.

728
00:47:47.990 --> 00:47:48.950
Well, you were looking into them,

729
00:47:48.950 --> 00:47:50.390
they were looking into you.

730
00:47:50.870 --> 00:47:53.270
All they had to do was fake an escape to get you here

731
00:47:53.270 --> 00:47:54.110
and now they're heavy.

732
00:47:54.110 --> 00:47:55.230
Now they have us both.

733
00:47:55.230 --> 00:47:56.070
Here, now.

734
00:48:00.230 --> 00:48:08.090
Marshal, are you out here wanting me in?

735
00:48:08.090 --> 00:48:08.930
What's wrong with us, huh?

736
00:48:08.930 --> 00:48:10.050
It's an island, boss.

737
00:48:10.050 --> 00:48:16.590
They're always gonna find us.

738
00:48:16.590 --> 00:48:18.990
This goddamn island, you and me.

739
00:48:18.990 --> 00:48:35.350
Come on.

740
00:48:35.350 --> 00:48:36.230
Get right off.

741
00:48:36.230 --> 00:48:37.910
Dr. Cawley wants to talk to you.

742
00:48:37.910 --> 00:48:39.270
Now.

743
00:48:39.270 --> 00:48:40.110
And hurry up.

744
00:48:40.110 --> 00:48:47.840
This thing is turning into a goddamn hurricane.

745
00:48:47.840 --> 00:48:50.160
I dropped those suits off to be cleaned.

746
00:48:50.160 --> 00:48:52.200
Should be ready by tomorrow.

747
00:48:52.240 --> 00:48:55.120
That is, if we all don't wash away first.

748
00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:56.200
You know, speaking of which,

749
00:48:56.200 --> 00:48:59.320
I'm afraid you're smoked, pretty much done for.

750
00:49:00.200 --> 00:49:02.970
So.

751
00:49:02.970 --> 00:49:05.210
This is our only choice, huh?

752
00:49:05.210 --> 00:49:06.930
That's something really nice in a prison grave,

753
00:49:06.930 --> 00:49:08.370
if that don't work for you.

754
00:49:08.370 --> 00:49:09.570
I know that you mention it.

755
00:49:09.570 --> 00:49:10.730
These are just fine.

756
00:49:12.010 --> 00:49:13.690
That's why I must repeat my insistence

757
00:49:13.690 --> 00:49:17.450
that all Ward C patients be placed in manual restraints.

758
00:49:17.450 --> 00:49:20.050
If the facility floods, they'll drown.

759
00:49:20.050 --> 00:49:21.290
You know that.

760
00:49:21.290 --> 00:49:22.570
That would take a lot of flooding.

761
00:49:22.610 --> 00:49:24.530
We're on an island in the middle of the ocean

762
00:49:24.530 --> 00:49:25.370
during a hurricane.

763
00:49:25.370 --> 00:49:28.050
A lot of flooding seems like a distinct possibility.

764
00:49:28.050 --> 00:49:29.450
It's a gamble, Stephen.

765
00:49:29.450 --> 00:49:30.570
Say the power fails.

766
00:49:30.570 --> 00:49:31.850
There's a backup generator.

767
00:49:31.850 --> 00:49:34.650
And if that goes, the cell doors will open.

768
00:49:36.090 --> 00:49:38.130
Where are they going to go?

769
00:49:38.130 --> 00:49:38.970
Hmm?

770
00:49:38.970 --> 00:49:39.810
They can't just hop a ferry,

771
00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:41.610
scoot over to the mainland and wreak havoc.

772
00:49:41.610 --> 00:49:42.610
You're quite right.

773
00:49:42.610 --> 00:49:46.690
They're far more likely to wreak havoc right here on us.

774
00:49:46.690 --> 00:49:49.010
If they're manacled to the floor, they'll die.

775
00:49:49.890 --> 00:49:52.290
There's 24 human beings.

776
00:49:52.850 --> 00:49:54.090
And you can live with that, can you?

777
00:49:54.090 --> 00:49:56.050
Frackly, if it were up to me.

778
00:49:56.050 --> 00:49:58.010
I'd put all 42 in wards A and B

779
00:49:58.010 --> 00:49:59.450
in manual restraints as well.

780
00:49:59.450 --> 00:50:01.610
Excuse me, excuse me.

781
00:50:01.610 --> 00:50:02.450
Marshal.

782
00:50:02.450 --> 00:50:05.090
I'm sorry, doctor, I just have one quick question.

783
00:50:05.090 --> 00:50:06.370
Yes, I'll be with you in a moment.

784
00:50:06.370 --> 00:50:09.390
We spoke this morning about Rachel Solando's note.

785
00:50:09.390 --> 00:50:11.170
The law of four, I love that.

786
00:50:11.170 --> 00:50:12.250
You said you had no idea

787
00:50:12.250 --> 00:50:14.910
what that second line could refer to, correct?

788
00:50:15.890 --> 00:50:17.850
Who is 67?

789
00:50:17.850 --> 00:50:19.530
Yes, I'm afraid I still don't.

790
00:50:19.530 --> 00:50:20.370
None of us do.

791
00:50:20.370 --> 00:50:21.690
Uh-huh.

792
00:50:21.690 --> 00:50:25.640
Nothing comes to mind.

793
00:50:25.640 --> 00:50:30.860
Nothing?

794
00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:32.200
Because I believe I just heard you say

795
00:50:32.200 --> 00:50:35.940
there are 24 patients in ward C

796
00:50:35.940 --> 00:50:38.500
and 42 patients in wards A and B,

797
00:50:38.500 --> 00:50:40.140
which means there's a total of what,

798
00:50:40.140 --> 00:50:42.060
66 patients at this facility?

799
00:50:43.640 --> 00:50:48.070
That is correct, yes.

800
00:50:48.070 --> 00:50:51.230
Well, it seems to me Rachel Solando is suggesting

801
00:50:51.230 --> 00:50:54.550
that you have a 67th patient doctor.

802
00:50:55.950 --> 00:50:57.950
But I'm afraid we don't.

803
00:50:57.950 --> 00:50:59.030
This is ridiculous.

804
00:50:59.030 --> 00:51:00.150
What are they doing here?

805
00:51:00.590 --> 00:51:02.510
They're doing a goddamn job.

806
00:51:02.510 --> 00:51:04.910
Didn't MacPherson tell you the good news?

807
00:51:06.350 --> 00:51:08.870
No, what's the good news, doctor?

808
00:51:08.870 --> 00:51:10.110
Rachel's been found.

809
00:51:11.630 --> 00:51:12.470
She's here.

810
00:51:14.170 --> 00:51:32.980
Safe and sound.

811
00:51:32.980 --> 00:51:39.490
Who are these men?

812
00:51:39.490 --> 00:51:41.170
Police officers, Rachel.

813
00:51:41.170 --> 00:51:52.060
They have a few questions.

814
00:51:52.060 --> 00:51:55.140
There has been a sighting of a known communist,

815
00:51:55.140 --> 00:52:00.460
subversive in this area, passing out literature.

816
00:52:00.460 --> 00:52:05.570
Here, in this neighborhood?

817
00:52:05.570 --> 00:52:08.750
Yes, I'm afraid so.

818
00:52:08.750 --> 00:52:10.870
Now, if you could tell us what you did yesterday

819
00:52:10.870 --> 00:52:13.250
where you were, it would really help us

820
00:52:13.250 --> 00:52:14.730
narrow down our search.

821
00:52:16.190 --> 00:52:32.240
Yes, well, I made breakfast for Jim and the children,

822
00:52:32.240 --> 00:52:38.120
packed Jim's lunch and he left,

823
