And now you're acting like.

1098
01:18:50.700 --> 01:18:51.700
Like what?

1099
01:18:51.700 --> 01:18:52.700
Like what?

1100
01:18:52.700 --> 01:18:57.860
How am I acting?

1101
01:18:57.860 --> 01:19:06.170
What the hell happened back there in those cells, Ted?

1102
01:19:06.170 --> 01:19:09.170
What do you think the weather's like in Portland, Chuck?

1103
01:19:09.170 --> 01:19:11.170
I'm from Seattle.

1104
01:19:11.170 --> 01:19:14.700
Seattle.

1105
01:19:14.700 --> 01:19:21.080
Alone.

1106
01:19:21.080 --> 01:19:25.480
I'm going with you, boss.

1107
01:19:25.480 --> 01:19:28.480
I said alone.

1108
01:19:28.480 --> 01:19:29.480
Fine.

1109
01:19:29.480 --> 01:20:07.380
I knew it wouldn't take long.

1110
01:20:07.380 --> 01:20:08.380
But I couldn't get to it.

1111
01:20:08.380 --> 01:20:09.380
The tide was up.

1112
01:20:09.380 --> 01:20:22.350
Chuck!

1113
01:20:22.350 --> 01:23:25.420
Teddy Daniels, I'm a cop.

1114
01:23:25.420 --> 01:23:26.420
You're the marshal.

1115
01:23:26.420 --> 01:23:28.860
That's right.

1116
01:23:28.860 --> 01:23:35.800
Would you mind taking your hand from behind your back, please?

1117
01:23:35.800 --> 01:23:36.800
Why?

1118
01:23:36.800 --> 01:23:37.800
Why?

1119
01:23:37.800 --> 01:23:41.150
I want to make sure that what you're holding won't hurt me.

1120
01:23:41.150 --> 01:24:12.150
I'm going to keep this, if you don't mind.

1121
01:24:12.150 --> 01:24:13.150
The real one.

1122
01:24:13.150 --> 01:24:19.110
Really your children.

1123
01:24:19.110 --> 01:24:23.440
Bad children.

1124
01:24:23.440 --> 01:24:26.980
I was never married.

1125
01:24:26.980 --> 01:24:30.980
And before I was a patient at Ashcliffe, I worked here.

1126
01:24:30.980 --> 01:24:41.240
You were a nurse?

1127
01:24:41.240 --> 01:24:42.240
You think I'm crazy?

1128
01:24:42.240 --> 01:24:45.070
Oh, no, I know.

1129
01:24:45.070 --> 01:25:02.410
And if I say I'm not crazy, then all your protests to the contrary just confirm what they're saying.

1130
01:25:02.410 --> 01:25:06.160
I'm not following you.

1131
01:25:06.160 --> 01:25:07.160
I'm sorry.

1132
01:25:07.160 --> 01:25:13.160
Once you're declared insane, then anything you do is called part of that insanity.

1133
01:25:13.160 --> 01:25:16.160
Reasonable protests or denial.

1134
01:25:16.160 --> 01:25:18.160
Valid fears.

1135
01:25:18.160 --> 01:25:19.160
Paranoia.

1136
01:25:19.160 --> 01:25:23.160
Survival instincts are defense mechanisms.

1137
01:25:23.160 --> 01:25:25.160
You're smarter than you look, marshal.

1138
01:25:25.160 --> 01:25:26.160
Probably not a good thing.

1139
01:25:26.160 --> 01:25:28.830
Tell me something.

1140
01:25:28.830 --> 01:25:39.200
I started asking about these large shipments of sodium amytal and opium-based hallucinogens.

1141
01:25:39.200 --> 01:25:41.200
Psychotropic drugs.

1142
01:25:41.200 --> 01:25:43.900
It's about the surgery.

1143
01:25:43.900 --> 01:25:50.480
It's part of the transorbital lobotomy.

1144
01:25:50.480 --> 01:25:56.480
These act the patient with electroshock and go through the eye with an ice pick.

1145
01:25:56.480 --> 01:26:03.540
Pull out some nerve fibers.

1146
01:26:03.540 --> 01:26:11.770
Makes the patient unconscionable.

1147
01:26:11.770 --> 01:26:16.370
You know how pain enters the body, marshal.

1148
01:26:16.370 --> 01:26:18.370
Do you?

1149
01:26:18.370 --> 01:26:20.370
Depends on where you're hurt.

1150
01:26:20.370 --> 01:26:21.370
No.

1151
01:26:21.370 --> 01:26:23.370
It has nothing to do with the flesh.

1152
01:26:23.370 --> 01:26:25.370
The brain controls pain.

1153
01:26:25.370 --> 01:26:30.370
The brain controls fear, empathy, sleep, hunger, anger, everything.

1154
01:26:30.370 --> 01:26:44.230
Recreate a man so he doesn't feel pain or love or sympathy.

1155
01:26:44.230 --> 01:26:49.230
A man who can't be interrogated because he has no memories to confess.

1156
01:26:49.230 --> 01:26:54.300
Take away all man's memories.

1157
01:26:54.300 --> 01:26:55.300
Never.

1158
01:26:56.300 --> 01:27:01.300
The North Koreans used American POWs during their brainwashing experiments.

1159
01:27:01.300 --> 01:27:03.300
They turned soldiers into traitors.

1160
01:27:03.300 --> 01:27:04.300
That's what they're doing here.

1161
01:27:04.300 --> 01:27:10.300
They're creating ghosts to go out in the world and do things sane men never would.

1162
01:27:10.300 --> 01:27:14.300
That kind of ability, that kind of knowledge, that would take years.

1163
01:27:14.300 --> 01:27:16.300
Years of research.

1164
01:27:16.300 --> 01:27:18.300
Hundreds of patients to experiment on.

1165
01:27:18.300 --> 01:27:23.580
Fifty years from now, people will look back and say,

1166
01:27:23.580 --> 01:27:26.580
Here, this place is where it all began.

1167
01:27:26.580 --> 01:27:28.580
The Nazis used the Jews.

1168
01:27:28.580 --> 01:27:30.580
Soviets used prisoners in their own gulags.

1169
01:27:30.580 --> 01:27:36.580
And we, we tested patients on Shutter Island.

1170
01:27:36.580 --> 01:27:38.580
No, they won't.

1171
01:27:38.580 --> 01:27:45.380
You do understand.

1172
01:27:45.380 --> 01:27:54.840
Royal Marshal, they can't stop me.

1173
01:27:54.840 --> 01:28:00.840
I was an esteemed psychiatrist from a respected family.

1174
01:28:00.840 --> 01:28:10.830
Let me ask you, any past traumas in your life?

1175
01:28:10.830 --> 01:28:17.340
Why, why would that matter?

1176
01:28:17.340 --> 01:28:22.340
Because they're going to point to some event in your past and say it's the reason you lost your sanity.

1177
01:28:22.340 --> 01:28:27.340
So that when they commit you here, your friends and colleagues will say,

1178
01:28:27.340 --> 01:28:31.000
Of course he cracked.

1179
01:28:31.000 --> 01:28:32.000
Who wouldn't after what he'd been through?

1180
01:28:32.000 --> 01:28:35.000
They can say that about anyone, anyone at all.

1181
01:28:35.000 --> 01:28:37.000
The point is they're going to say it about you.

1182
01:28:37.000 --> 01:28:44.920
My head?

1183
01:28:44.920 --> 01:28:46.920
Any funny dreams lately?

1184
01:28:46.920 --> 01:28:53.490
Trouble sleeping?

1185
01:28:53.490 --> 01:28:55.490
I am prone to migraines, yes.

1186
01:28:55.490 --> 01:29:05.740
Jesus.

1187
01:29:05.740 --> 01:29:08.740
And you, you ate the food in the cafeteria and drunk the coffee they gave you.

1188
01:29:08.740 --> 01:29:20.030
You tell me at least that you've been smoking your own cigarettes.

1189
01:29:20.030 --> 01:29:27.370
It takes 36 to 48 hours for neuroleptic narcotics to reach workable levels in the bloodstream.

1190
01:29:27.370 --> 01:29:29.370
Policy comes first.

1191
01:29:29.370 --> 01:29:34.260
First the fingertips, then eventually the whole hand.

1192
01:29:34.260 --> 01:29:37.260
Seen any walking nightmares lately, Marshal?

1193
01:29:37.260 --> 01:29:47.170
Tell me what goes on in that lighthouse.

1194
01:29:47.170 --> 01:29:49.170
Brain surgery.

1195
01:29:49.170 --> 01:29:52.170
Well, let's open the skull and see what happens if we pull on this kind.

1196
01:29:52.170 --> 01:29:55.680
They learned it from the Nazis kind.

1197
01:29:55.680 --> 01:30:04.810
Who knows about this?

1198
01:30:04.810 --> 01:30:06.810
On the island, I mean, who?

1199
01:30:06.810 --> 01:30:14.520
The nurses? The, the, the, the orderlies?

1200
01:30:14.520 --> 01:30:16.520
They couldn't possibly know me.

1201
01:30:16.520 --> 01:30:17.520
Everyone.

1202
01:30:17.520 --> 01:30:39.070
You can't stay here.

1203
01:30:39.070 --> 01:30:43.070
They think I'm dead, that I drown. I'm afraid if they come looking for you, they might find me.

1204
01:30:43.070 --> 01:30:45.070
I'm sorry, but you have to go.

1205
01:30:45.070 --> 01:30:54.040
I'm going to come back for you.

1206
01:30:54.040 --> 01:30:57.040
I won't be here. I move during the day, new places every night.

1207
01:30:57.040 --> 01:31:00.040
But I could come get you, get you off this island.

1208
01:31:00.040 --> 01:31:02.040
Haven't you heard a word I said?

1209
01:31:02.040 --> 01:31:06.040
The only way off the island is a ferry, and they control it.

1210
01:31:06.040 --> 01:31:08.040
You'll never leave here.

1211
01:31:08.040 --> 01:31:19.870
I had a friend.

1212
01:31:19.870 --> 01:31:22.870
I was with him yesterday, but we got separated.

1213
01:31:22.870 --> 01:31:24.870
Have you seen him?

1214
01:31:24.870 --> 01:31:31.000
Marshal, you have no friends.

1215
01:31:31.000 --> 01:32:05.710
There you are.

1216
01:32:05.710 --> 01:32:12.700
We were wondering when you'd show up.

1217
01:32:12.700 --> 01:32:14.700
Have a seat.

1218
01:32:14.700 --> 01:32:15.700
Come in.

1219
01:32:15.700 --> 01:32:30.550
Taking a leisurely stroll, were we?

1220
01:32:30.550 --> 01:32:33.550
I was, uh, just, just looking around.

1221
01:32:33.550 --> 01:32:38.170
Did you enjoy God's latest gift?

1222
01:32:38.170 --> 01:32:40.870
What?

1223
01:32:40.870 --> 01:32:45.440
God's gift. The violence.

1224
01:32:45.440 --> 01:32:55.120
When I came downstairs in my home, and I saw that tree in my living room, it reached out for me.

1225
01:32:55.120 --> 01:32:58.820
A divine hand.

1226
01:32:58.820 --> 01:33:03.280
God loves violence.

1227
01:33:03.280 --> 01:33:05.280
I, I hadn't noticed.

1228
01:33:05.280 --> 01:33:07.280
Sure you have.

1229
01:33:07.280 --> 01:33:09.280
Why else would there be so much of it?

1230
01:33:09.280 --> 01:33:11.280
It's in us.

1231
01:33:11.280 --> 01:33:14.690
It's what we are.

1232
01:33:14.690 --> 01:33:19.690
We wage war, and we burn sacrifices, and pillage and plunder, and tear at the flesh of our brothers, and why?

1233
01:33:19.690 --> 01:33:23.690
Because God gave us violence to wage in his honor.

1234
01:33:23.690 --> 01:33:28.540
I thought God gave us moral order.

1235
01:33:28.540 --> 01:33:32.540
There's no moral order as pure as this storm.

1236
01:33:32.540 --> 01:33:34.540
There's no moral order at all.

1237
01:33:34.540 --> 01:33:36.540
There's just this.

1238
01:33:36.540 --> 01:33:38.540
Can my violence conquer yours?

1239
01:33:38.540 --> 01:33:45.110
I'm not violent.

1240
01:33:45.110 --> 01:33:47.110
Yes, you are.

1241
01:33:47.110 --> 01:33:50.110
You're as violent as they come.

1242
01:33:50.110 --> 01:33:54.110
I know this because I'm as violent as they come.

1243
01:33:54.110 --> 01:33:59.110
The constraints of society were lifted, and I was all that stood between you and a meal.

1244
01:33:59.110 --> 01:34:05.640
You would crack my skull with a rock and eat my meaty parts, wouldn't you?

1245
01:34:05.640 --> 01:34:13.720
Carly thinks you're harmless, that you can be controlled, but I know different.

1246
01:34:13.720 --> 01:34:15.720
You don't know me.

1247
01:34:15.720 --> 01:34:16.720
Oh, but I do.

1248
01:34:16.720 --> 01:34:18.720
Oh, I know you.

1249
01:34:19.720 --> 01:34:31.860
We've known each other for centuries.

1250
01:34:31.860 --> 01:34:42.180
If I was to sink my teeth into your eye right now, would you be able to stop me before I blinded you?

1251
01:34:42.180 --> 01:34:43.180
Give it a try.

1252
01:34:43.180 --> 01:35:34.270
That's the spirit.

1253
01:35:34.270 --> 01:35:35.270
Where have you been?

1254
01:35:35.270 --> 01:35:41.690
Oh, I forgot you're leaving, now that Rachel's been found.

1255
01:35:41.690 --> 01:35:49.070
For sure, yeah. Big meaning.

1256
01:35:49.070 --> 01:35:55.690
Apparently there was an unidentified man in Ward C yesterday.

1257
01:35:55.690 --> 01:35:58.690
He subdued a highly dangerous patient quite handily.

1258
01:35:59.690 --> 01:36:00.690
Hey, that's all.

1259
01:36:00.690 --> 01:36:03.690
He usually had a long conversation with a paranoid schizophrenic, George Noyce.

1260
01:36:03.690 --> 01:36:12.680
This Noyce, he said his name was, he's, uh, delusional.

1261
01:36:12.680 --> 01:36:15.680
Oh, extremely. It can be quite upsetting.

1262
01:36:15.680 --> 01:36:21.680
As a matter of fact, two weeks ago, a patient got so wound up by one of Noyce's stories that he beat him up.

1263
01:36:21.680 --> 01:36:24.350
Cigarette.

1264
01:36:24.350 --> 01:36:31.370
So, you're taking the ferry?

1265
01:36:31.370 --> 01:36:36.370
Yes, absolutely. I, uh, I think we've gotten all we came here for, so...

1266
01:36:37.370 --> 01:36:38.370
We, Marshal?

1267
01:36:38.370 --> 01:36:43.320
Speaking of which, have you seen him, Doctor?

1268
01:36:43.320 --> 01:36:44.320
Whom?

1269
01:36:45.320 --> 01:36:47.320
My partner, Chuck.

1270
01:36:47.320 --> 01:36:52.530
You don't have a partner, Marshal. You came here alone.

1271
01:36:52.530 --> 01:37:01.000
You know, I've built something valuable here, and valuable things have a way of being misunderstood in their own time.

1272
01:37:01.000 --> 01:37:03.000
Everyone wants a quick fix. They always have.

1273
01:37:03.000 --> 01:37:09.000
I'm trying to do something that people, yourself included, don't understand, and I'm not going to give up without a fight.

1274
01:37:09.000 --> 01:37:12.360
I can see that.

1275
01:37:12.360 --> 01:37:18.680
So tell me again about your partner.

1276
01:37:18.680 --> 01:37:22.150
What partner?

1277
01:37:22.150 --> 01:38:31.760
Going somewhere?

1278
01:38:32.760 --> 01:38:35.760
No, I'm just, uh, heading out to the ferry, so...

1279
01:38:35.760 --> 01:38:39.760
Ah, I'm afraid, I'm afraid it's the other way.

1280
01:38:39.760 --> 01:38:47.670
If you'll wait a moment, I'll find you someone who can take you to the dock.

1281
01:38:51.290 --> 01:38:55.020
Huh? What's this?

1282
01:38:55.020 --> 01:38:58.020
It's just a sedative. Precaution.

1283
01:38:58.020 --> 01:38:59.020
Oh, precaution.

1284
01:39:02.020 --> 01:39:05.020
What are you going to do? Kill me?

1285
01:39:06.020 --> 01:39:07.020
Marshal.

1286
01:39:07.020 --> 01:39:09.020
You think you deserve it?

1287
01:39:09.020 --> 01:39:12.020
For what, hmm? Provoking you?

1288
01:39:12.020 --> 01:39:16.020
Well, forgive me. What doesn't provoke you?

1289
01:39:16.020 --> 01:39:18.020
Remarks? Words?

1290
01:39:18.020 --> 01:39:19.020
Nazis?

1291
01:39:19.020 --> 01:39:24.020
Well, that too. And of course memories and dreams.

1292
01:39:24.020 --> 01:39:29.020
Did you know that the word trauma comes from the Greek for wound?

1293
01:39:29.020 --> 01:39:32.020
And what is the German word for dream?

1294
01:39:32.020 --> 01:39:33.020
Thaum.

1295
01:39:33.020 --> 01:39:35.020
I like thaum.

1296
01:39:36.020 --> 01:39:42.020
Wounds can create monsters, and you, you are wounded, Marshal.

1297
01:39:43.020 --> 01:39:48.020
And wouldn't you agree, when you see a monster, you must stop it.

1298
01:39:50.020 --> 01:40:02.250
Yes.

1299
01:40:16.510 --> 01:40:19.850
How long you been on the clock?

1300
01:40:19.850 --> 01:40:21.850
Been on for 18 hours straight.

1301
01:40:21.850 --> 01:40:23.850
Nice paycheck.

1302
01:40:40.400 --> 01:40:48.460
What are you doing, baby? You gotta get to the ferry.

1303
01:40:48.460 --> 01:40:59.570
If the world thinks that Chuck is dead, then he's perfect for their experiments.

1304
01:41:00.570 --> 01:41:02.570
There's only one place they'd take him.

1305
01:41:02.570 --> 01:41:07.070
You go there and you'll die.

1306
01:41:07.070 --> 01:41:12.070
He's my partner. If they are hurting him, if they're holding him against his will, I've gotta bring him out.

1307
01:41:12.070 --> 01:41:14.070
I can't lose anyone else.

1308
01:41:14.070 --> 01:41:18.070
Don't go, Teddy. Please, please don't do this. Don't go.

1309
01:41:18.070 --> 01:41:27.890
I'm sorry, honey. I love this thing because you gave it to me.

1310
01:41:27.890 --> 01:41:36.560
The truth is, it was one fucking ugly tie.

1311
01:41:36.560 --> 01:45:43.780
You're all wet, baby.

1312
01:45:43.780 --> 01:45:46.920
What did you say?

1313
01:45:46.920 --> 01:45:48.920
You know exactly what I said.

1314
01:45:48.920 --> 01:46:12.120
The rifle's empty, by the way. Have a seat.

1315
01:46:12.120 --> 01:46:23.500
For God's sake, dry off. You'll catch a cold.

1316
01:46:23.500 --> 01:46:28.310
All right.

1317
01:46:28.310 --> 01:46:37.890
How badly did you hurt the guard?

1318
01:46:37.890 --> 01:46:38.890
Yes, he's here.

1319
01:46:39.890 --> 01:46:42.890
Have Dr. Sheehan take a look at your man before you send him up.

1320
01:46:43.890 --> 01:46:48.890
So, Dr. Sheehan came in on the ferry this morning, huh?

1321
01:46:49.890 --> 01:46:50.890
Not exactly.

1322
01:46:51.890 --> 01:46:54.890
You blew up my car. I really love that car.

1323
01:46:54.890 --> 01:47:03.360
Tremors are getting pretty bad.

1324
01:47:04.360 --> 01:47:06.360
How are the hallucinations?

1325
01:47:06.360 --> 01:47:08.360
Get out of here, Teddy.

1326
01:47:09.360 --> 01:47:11.360
This place is going to be the end of you.

1327
01:47:11.360 --> 01:47:16.930
They'll get worse.

1328
01:47:16.930 --> 01:47:24.160
Dr. Solando told me about the neuroleptics.

1329
01:47:24.160 --> 01:47:27.160
Did she know? And when was this?

1330
01:47:27.160 --> 01:47:33.160
I found a doctor in a cave out by the cliffs, but he'll never get to her.

1331
01:47:33.160 --> 01:47:37.160
I don't doubt it, considering she's not real.

1332
01:47:37.160 --> 01:47:40.850
Your delusions are more severe than I thought.

1333
01:47:40.850 --> 01:47:44.610
You're not on neuroleptics.

1334
01:47:45.610 --> 01:47:47.610
You're not on anything, as a matter of fact.

1335
01:47:47.610 --> 01:47:50.610
Then what the fuck is this, huh? What the fuck is this?

1336
01:47:50.610 --> 01:47:51.610
Withdrawal.

1337
01:47:51.610 --> 01:47:53.610
Withdrawal?

1338
01:47:53.610 --> 01:47:56.610
From what? I haven't had a goddamn drink since I've been on this island.

1339
01:47:56.610 --> 01:47:58.610
Chlorpromazine.

1340
01:47:59.610 --> 01:48:02.610
I'm not a fan of pharmacology, but I have to say, in your case...

1341
01:48:02.610 --> 01:48:04.610
Chlor... chloro... chloro... what?

1342
01:48:04.610 --> 01:48:06.610
Chlorpromazine.

1343
01:48:06.610 --> 01:48:10.610
The same thing we've been giving you for the past 24 months.

1344
01:48:11.610 --> 01:48:17.610
So for the past two years, you've had somebody slipping me drugs in Boston, is that it?

1345
01:48:17.610 --> 01:48:20.610
Not Boston. Here.

1346
01:48:21.610 --> 01:48:25.610
You've been here for two years. A patient of this institution.

1347
01:48:25.610 --> 01:48:31.880
After everything I've seen here, doctor.

1348
01:48:31.880 --> 01:48:35.880
You really think you're going to convince me I'm crazy, huh?

1349
01:48:35.880 --> 01:48:37.880
Do you know the kind of people that I deal with every day?

1350
01:48:37.880 --> 01:48:39.880
I'm a U.S. Marshal, for God's sakes.

1351
01:48:39.880 --> 01:48:41.880
You were a U.S. Marshal.

1352
01:48:41.880 --> 01:48:45.880
Here's a copy of the intake form you broke in towards C4.

1353
01:48:45.880 --> 01:48:47.880
Proof of the 67th patient.

1354
01:48:47.880 --> 01:48:50.880
If you'd gotten it to the mainland, you could have blown the lid off this place.

1355
01:48:50.880 --> 01:48:53.880
Somehow you couldn't find time to look at it.

1356
01:48:53.880 --> 01:48:55.880
Well, read it now.

1357
01:48:55.880 --> 01:48:56.880
Go ahead.

1358
01:48:56.880 --> 01:49:05.100
Patient is highly intelligent, highly delusional, decorated army veteran.

1359
01:49:05.100 --> 01:49:08.100
Present for the liberation of Dachau.

1360
01:49:09.100 --> 01:49:16.100
Former U.S. Marshal. Known proclivity for violence shows no remorse for his crime because he denies the crime ever took place.

1361
01:49:16.100 --> 01:49:21.100
Highly developed and fantastical. Narratives which preclude facing the truth of his actions.

1362
01:49:21.100 --> 01:49:25.100
I've had enough of this bullshit. Where's my partner, huh? Where's Chuck? Where is he?

1363
01:49:25.100 --> 01:49:27.100
Let's try this another way.

1364
01:49:27.100 --> 01:49:30.100
Your wife's maiden name was Chanal, am I correct?

1365
01:49:30.100 --> 01:49:32.100
Don't you even talk about her, don't you?

1366
01:49:32.100 --> 01:49:33.100
I'm afraid I have to.

1367
01:49:34.100 --> 01:49:36.100
Notice anything these four names have in common?

1368
01:49:36.100 --> 01:49:39.100
It's your rule of four, Andrew. What do you see?

1369
01:49:39.100 --> 01:49:42.100
If you've done anything to my partner, doctor, that is a violation of faith.

1370
01:49:42.100 --> 01:49:45.100
Focus, Andrew. What do you see?

1371
01:49:45.100 --> 01:49:48.100
The names have the same letters.

1372
01:49:48.100 --> 01:49:55.100
Edward Daniels has exactly the same 13 letters as Andrew Ladis, the same as Rachel Solando and Dolores Chanal.

1373
01:49:55.100 --> 01:49:57.100
The names are anagrams for each other.

1374
01:49:57.100 --> 01:50:00.100
Yeah, yeah, tactics. They're not gonna work on you.

1375
01:50:00.100 --> 01:50:02.100
You came here for the truth.

1376
01:50:02.100 --> 01:50:07.100
Here it is. Your name is Andrew Ladis, the 67th patient at Ashcliffe.

1377
01:50:07.100 --> 01:50:09.100
He's you, Andrew.

1378
01:50:09.100 --> 01:50:10.100
Shit.

1379
01:50:10.100 --> 01:50:14.790
You were committed here by court order 24 months ago.

1380
01:50:14.790 --> 01:50:19.790
Your crime is terrible, one you can't forgive yourself for, so you invented another self.

1381
01:50:19.790 --> 01:50:20.790
Down to the facts.

1382
01:50:20.790 --> 01:50:31.930
You've created a story in which you're not a murderer, you're a hero, still a US marshal.

1383
01:50:31.930 --> 01:50:33.930
Only here at Ashcliffe because of a case.

1384
01:50:33.930 --> 01:50:38.930
And you've uncovered a conspiracy so that anything we tell you about who you are, what you've done,

1385
01:50:38.930 --> 01:50:40.930
you can dismiss his lies, Andrew.

1386
01:50:40.930 --> 01:50:42.930
My name is Edward Daniels.

1387
01:50:42.930 --> 01:50:46.930
I've been here in this fantasy for two years now. I know every detail.

1388
01:50:46.930 --> 01:50:52.930
Patient 67, the storm, Rachel Solando, your missing partner, the dreams you have every night.

1389
01:50:52.930 --> 01:50:55.930
You were a dachau, but you may not have killed any guards.

1390
01:50:55.930 --> 01:51:02.400
I wish I could let you just live in your fantasy world.

1391
01:51:02.400 --> 01:51:04.400
I really do.

1392
01:51:04.400 --> 01:51:09.400
But you're violent, trained, dangerous. You're the most dangerous patient we have.

1393
01:51:09.400 --> 01:51:14.400
You've injured orderless guards, other patients. Two weeks ago, you attacked George Noyce.

1394
01:51:14.400 --> 01:51:17.400
No, no, I am fucking on to you, doctor. You had Noyce beaten.

1395
01:51:17.400 --> 01:51:18.400
Of course I didn't.

1396
01:51:18.400 --> 01:51:20.400
Give me one reason why I would even touch him.

1397
01:51:20.400 --> 01:51:25.400
Because he called you Ladis, and you'd do anything not to be him.

1398
01:51:25.400 --> 01:51:29.400
I have a transcript of the conversation you had with Noyce yesterday.

1399
01:51:29.400 --> 01:51:33.400
This is about you, and Ladis, that's all it's ever been about.

1400
01:51:33.400 --> 01:51:38.670
He's saying this is about me and Ladis.

1401
01:51:38.670 --> 01:51:42.670
When you asked him what happened to his face, he said, and I hear I'm quoting again,

1402
01:51:42.670 --> 01:51:43.670
you did this.

1403
01:51:43.670 --> 01:51:46.670
No, no, he meant that it was my fault.

1404
01:51:46.670 --> 01:51:47.670
You almost killed him.

1405
01:51:47.670 --> 01:51:53.400
The warden and the board of overseers are determined something be done.

1406
01:51:53.400 --> 01:51:58.400
It's been decided that unless we can bring you back to sanity now, right now,

1407
01:51:58.400 --> 01:52:03.400
permanent measures will be taken to ensure you can't hurt anyone ever again.

1408
01:52:03.400 --> 01:52:09.440
They'll lobotomize you, Andrew. Do you understand?

1409
01:52:09.440 --> 01:52:22.610
If I don't play along with your little game here,

1410
01:52:22.610 --> 01:52:26.610
Dr. Naring's going to turn me into one of his ghosts.

1411
01:52:26.610 --> 01:52:28.610
What about my partner?

1412
01:52:28.610 --> 01:52:32.610
You're going to tell the U.S. Marshal's office that he's a defense mechanism?

1413
01:52:32.610 --> 01:52:35.630
Hello, boss.

1414
01:52:35.630 --> 01:53:03.200
Working for him?

1415
01:53:03.200 --> 01:53:07.200
I'm sorry, there wasn't any other way. Someone had to stick with you, keep you safe.

1416
01:53:07.200 --> 01:53:15.680
You mean watch me, huh? Watch me every minute.

1417
01:53:15.680 --> 01:53:19.960
Who are you? Who are you? Tell me.

1418
01:53:19.960 --> 01:53:22.960
Don't you recognize me, Andrew?

1419
01:53:22.960 --> 01:53:26.960
I've been your primary psychiatrist for the last two years.

1420
01:53:26.960 --> 01:53:28.960
I'm Lester Sheehan.

1421
01:53:28.960 --> 01:53:29.960
I know.

1422
01:53:29.960 --> 01:53:40.790
I climbed down a cliff. I trusted you.

1423
01:53:40.790 --> 01:53:45.320
I risked everything to come in here after you.

1424
01:53:45.320 --> 01:53:46.320
Everything!

1425
01:53:46.320 --> 01:53:47.320
I know, boss.

1426
01:53:47.320 --> 01:53:49.320
We're running out of time here, Andrew.

1427
01:53:49.320 --> 01:53:54.320
I swore before the board of overseers that I could construct the most radical,

1428
01:53:54.320 --> 01:53:57.320
cutting-edge role play ever attempted in psychiatry,

1429
01:53:57.320 --> 01:53:58.320
and it would bring you back.

1430
01:53:58.320 --> 01:54:03.320
I thought that if we let you play this out, we could get you to see how untrue,

1431
01:54:03.320 --> 01:54:05.320
how impossible it is.

1432
01:54:05.320 --> 01:54:08.320
You've had the run of the place for two days.

1433
01:54:08.320 --> 01:54:12.320
Tell me, where are the Nazi experiments?

1434
01:54:12.320 --> 01:54:14.320
The satanic awards.

1435
01:54:14.320 --> 01:54:15.320
Listen to me.

1436
01:54:15.320 --> 01:54:37.710
If we fail with you, then everything that we've tried to do here will be discredited, everything.

1437
01:54:37.710 --> 01:54:42.140
We're on the front lines of a war here, old boy.

1438
01:54:42.140 --> 01:54:46.680
And right now, it'll come down to you.

1439
01:54:46.680 --> 01:54:47.680
It'll come down to you.

1440
01:54:47.680 --> 01:54:56.130
Move them out!

1441
01:54:56.130 --> 01:54:58.130
Andrew, Andrew, no, no.

1442
01:54:58.130 --> 01:55:01.130
My name is Edward Daniels.

1443
01:55:01.130 --> 01:55:02.130
This one's loaded.

1444
01:55:02.130 --> 01:55:03.130
I can tell by the weight.

1445
01:55:03.130 --> 01:55:06.130
I see, and that's your firearm, Marshal? You're sure?

1446
01:55:06.130 --> 01:55:07.130
My initials are on the side.

1447
01:55:07.130 --> 01:55:10.130
There's a dent in the barrel from when Philip Stacks shot at me.

1448
01:55:10.130 --> 01:55:12.130
You're not going to fuck with my mind on this one, doctor.

1449
01:55:12.130 --> 01:55:23.170
Then blast away, because that's the only way you're ever getting off this island.

1450
01:55:23.170 --> 01:55:24.170
Drew, please don't.

1451
01:55:24.170 --> 01:55:45.660
What did you do to my goddamn gun?

1452
01:55:45.660 --> 01:55:47.660
It's a toy, Andrew.

1453
01:55:47.660 --> 01:55:52.570
We're telling you the truth.

1454
01:55:53.570 --> 01:55:57.570
Dolores was insane, manic-depressive, suicidal.

1455
01:55:57.570 --> 01:56:00.570
You drank, stayed away, ignored what everyone told you.

1456
01:56:00.570 --> 01:56:05.570
You moved to that lake house after she purposely set your city apartment on fire.

1457
01:56:05.570 --> 01:56:09.570
You're lying!

1458
01:56:09.570 --> 01:56:11.570
All you've done is lie!

1459
01:56:11.570 --> 01:56:14.570
Andrew, your children, Andrew, your children.

1460
01:56:14.570 --> 01:56:17.570
Simon, Henry.

1461
01:56:17.570 --> 01:56:19.570
We never had any children.

1462
01:56:19.570 --> 01:56:23.570
Your wife drowned them at the cabin by the lake.

1463
01:56:23.570 --> 01:56:28.570
And here, the little girl, the one you dream of every night.

1464
01:56:28.570 --> 01:56:30.570
We never had a little girl.

1465
01:56:30.570 --> 01:56:35.570
The one who tells you over and over that you should have saved her, saved them all.

1466
01:56:35.570 --> 01:56:38.570
Your daughter, her name was Rachel.

1467
01:56:38.570 --> 01:56:41.570
Are you going to deny that she ever lived?

1468
01:56:41.570 --> 01:56:43.570
Andrew, are you?

1469
01:56:43.570 --> 01:57:16.400
I told you not to come in here.

1470
01:57:16.400 --> 01:57:17.400
I told you.

1471
01:57:17.400 --> 01:57:42.150
I'm back.

1472
01:57:42.150 --> 01:57:45.150
We got him just outside of Oklahoma.

1473
01:57:45.150 --> 01:57:48.150
Must have stopped ten places in between here and Tulsa.

1474
01:57:48.150 --> 01:57:54.210
I could sleep for a week.

1475
01:57:54.210 --> 01:58:10.920
Dolores? Dolores?

1476
01:58:10.920 --> 01:58:14.920
Dolores?

1477
01:58:14.920 --> 01:58:27.160
Dolores?

1478
01:58:27.160 --> 01:58:57.740
Baby, why are you all wet?

1479
01:58:57.740 --> 01:59:02.040
I missed you.

1480
01:59:02.040 --> 01:59:10.750
You want to go home?

1481
01:59:10.750 --> 01:59:21.320
You are home.

1482
01:59:21.320 --> 01:59:26.140
Where are the kids?

1483
01:59:26.140 --> 01:59:28.140
They're in school.

1484
01:59:28.140 --> 01:59:35.780
It's Saturday, honey.

1485
01:59:35.780 --> 01:59:37.780
School's not in on Saturday.

1486
01:59:37.780 --> 01:59:42.370
My school is.

1487
01:59:42.370 --> 02:00:27.880
Come on, come on.

1488
02:00:27.880 --> 02:00:44.640
No, please.

1489
02:00:44.640 --> 02:00:45.640
Cut.

1490
02:00:45.640 --> 02:00:48.880
Cut.

1491
02:00:48.880 --> 02:00:57.020
No.

1492
02:00:57.020 --> 02:02:11.140
Put them in the tape.

1493
02:02:11.140 --> 02:02:14.760
Dry them off.

1494
02:02:14.760 --> 02:02:16.760
We'll change their clothes.

1495
02:02:16.760 --> 02:02:21.520
They'll be our living dolls.

1496
02:02:21.520 --> 02:02:34.360
Careful, Mom.

1497
02:02:34.360 --> 02:03:16.270
I love you so much.

1498
02:03:16.270 --> 02:03:49.050
I love you.

1499
02:03:49.050 --> 02:03:50.050
Andrew.

1500
02:03:50.050 --> 02:03:54.230
Andrew, can you hear me?

1501
02:03:54.230 --> 02:03:55.230
Rachel.

1502
02:03:55.230 --> 02:03:57.700
Rachel.

1503
02:03:57.700 --> 02:03:58.700
Rachel.

1504
02:03:58.700 --> 02:04:01.720
Rachel?

1505
02:04:01.720 --> 02:04:17.890
Rachel who?

1506
02:04:17.890 --> 02:04:18.890
Why are you here?

1507
02:04:18.890 --> 02:04:23.670
Because I killed my wife.

1508
02:04:23.670 --> 02:04:25.670
And why did you do that?

1509
02:04:25.670 --> 02:04:32.490
She murdered our children.

1510
02:04:32.490 --> 02:04:37.370
She told me to let her go.

1511
02:04:37.370 --> 02:04:43.180
Who's Teddy Daniels?

1512
02:04:43.180 --> 02:04:47.000
He doesn't exist.

1513
02:04:47.000 --> 02:04:48.000
Now that is Rachel Solando.

1514
02:04:48.000 --> 02:04:49.000
I made them up.

1515
02:04:49.000 --> 02:04:50.000
Why?

1516
02:04:50.000 --> 02:04:53.480
We need to hear you say it.

1517
02:04:53.480 --> 02:05:09.350
For the first time, Dolores told me she had an insect.

1518
02:05:09.350 --> 02:05:22.860
It's just for fun.

1519
02:05:22.860 --> 02:05:41.110
Why did you make them up?

1520
02:05:41.110 --> 02:05:47.180
Because I can't take knowing that Dolores killed our children.

1521
02:05:47.180 --> 02:06:12.410
Here's my fear, Andrew.

1522
02:06:12.410 --> 02:06:17.410
We broke through once before, nine months ago, and then you regressed.

1523
02:06:17.410 --> 02:06:30.200
You reset, Andrew, like a tape playing over and over on an endless loop.

1524
02:06:30.200 --> 02:06:35.200
I hope that what we've done here will be enough to stop it from ever happening again,

1525
02:06:35.200 --> 02:06:39.200
but I need to know you've accepted reality.

1526
02:06:39.200 --> 02:06:47.950
You came after me, huh, Doctor?

1527
02:06:47.950 --> 02:07:19.840
He tried to help me when no one else would, and I murdered my wife in the spring of 52.

1528
02:07:19.840 --> 02:07:47.090
How are we doing this morning?

1529
02:07:47.090 --> 02:07:48.090
Good.

1530
02:07:48.090 --> 02:07:49.090
And you?

1531
02:07:49.090 --> 02:07:51.090
Can't complain.

1532
02:07:51.090 --> 02:08:03.880
So what's our next move?

1533
02:08:03.880 --> 02:08:04.880
You tell me.

1534
02:08:04.880 --> 02:08:13.100
I gotta get off this rock, Chuck.

1535
02:08:13.100 --> 02:08:17.100
Get back to the mainland, whatever the hell's going on here, it's bad.

1536
02:08:17.100 --> 02:08:41.680
Let me catch us.

1537
02:08:41.680 --> 02:08:50.470
That's right, we're too smart for them.

1538
02:08:50.470 --> 02:08:54.040
Yeah, we are, aren't we?

1539
02:08:54.040 --> 02:09:13.290
You know, this place makes me wonder.

1540
02:09:13.290 --> 02:09:15.290
Yeah, what's that, boss?

1541
02:09:15.290 --> 02:09:23.570
Which would be worse, to live as a monster or to die as a good man?

1542
02:09:23.570 --> 02:09:34.820
Teddy?

